WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.856
We called this the Stentrode.

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:05.279
For people&nbsp;with paralysis,
this is a return to life.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.735
Graham Felstead, an incredible 
human being suffering&nbsp;with ALS,

00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:12.877
became the first person 
in the world to receive

00:00:12.877 --> 00:00:15.372
and use one of these 
brain-computer&nbsp;interfaces.

00:00:15.372 --> 00:00:18.765
Once it's in place, it's connected
to this tiny antenna

00:00:18.765 --> 00:00:20.854
that sits under the 
skin in the&nbsp;chest.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:25.053
This collects the raw brain data 
and sends it out of the body

00:00:25.053 --> 00:00:28.530
wirelessly to then connect 
with&nbsp;external devices.

00:00:28.893 --> 00:00:30.912
It's kind of like learning 
how to ride a bike.

00:00:30.912 --> 00:00:33.608
It takes a bit of practice, 
but once&nbsp;you're rolling,

00:00:33.608 --> 00:00:34.804
it becomes natural.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.789
Now I just look on the 
screen where I want to click

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:40.824
and I'm&nbsp;texting, messaging 
the world via Twitter.

00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:45.244
Graham, he said, as his 
ALS was progressing,

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.412
that it&nbsp;gave him immense 
comfort to know that

00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:49.977
even if his body was failing,

00:00:49.977 --> 00:00:51.275
he was always going to&nbsp;be able

00:00:51.275 --> 00:00:53.353
to tell his wife that he loved her.

